  "costUsd": null,
  "content": "Owen's approach play is below the team and the Tour. Against his level, only greens in regulation can be compared, because strokes gained has no college figure.\n\n**Strokes gained: approach.** Over his newest rounds, which are 8 recorded rounds from June 9 to September 26, he is at -4.16 strokes per round.\n- Level: no college figure.\n- Team: the team average is -2.33, and he is last of 7 on the team.\n- Tour: the PGA Tour baseline is 0.\n\n**Greens in regulation.** He hit 61.11% over 144 holes in the same window.\n- Level: the Division I average is 60%. He is slightly above it, at 36th percentile among 71 college players.\n- Team: the team average is 66.25%, and he sits at the 17th percentile of 7.\n- Tour: the PGA Tour figure is 66%.\n\nAcross all his recorded rounds, GIR is 61.57% and approach strokes gained is -3.83. So the pattern holds over the longer record.\n\nHis greens-hit rate is about at the Division I average, but he loses a lot of strokes on approach. That suggests the cost is in shot quality: where the ball finishes, and the misses that cost strokes. It is not the number of greens he hits. The data above can't show which of those it is. Proximity by distance band would be the next read.",
